+/// SecondSonPC (P3.4, patch 0022): SecondSonPC's exception dispatcher owns the process's vectored
+/// exception handler and calls the bridge's handlers itself (DispatchAccessViolation for the GPU write
+/// tracking and the SRT walker, DispatchIllegalInstruction for the CPU patcher, HandlePatchBreakpoint).
+/// Then SignalDispatch registers no handler of its own, and RemoveHandlers (an assert failing in the
+/// bridge) calls `on_remove` instead. Call before the first Signals::Instance().
+void UseExternalExceptionDispatch(void (*on_remove)());
+bool ExternalExceptionDispatch();
